%description:

TcpVegas.gamma:other -- slow start ends with more than the value of extra segments.

The claim (TcpVegas.ned): "in slow start, above this many extra segments, Vegas leaves slow
start".

The classes: linux (1, the default, the value of Linux tcp_vegas.c), other (a larger value),
invalid (below 0). The code: once
each round trip, TcpVegas::receivedAckForUnackedData() compares the extra segments, diff,
with the thresholds; TcpVegas::initializeAlgorithm() checks them. In slow start, the window grows only in each second round
trip. This test separates "other" from "linux".

Host under test: host1, with TcpVegas, which sends to host2 in slow start; the path
is host1 -- tap -- router -- host2, with a bottleneck of 10 Mbps from the router to host2 and
a round trip of 40 ms, so the path holds 34 segments; host2 has no delayed ACK
(precondition: a delayed ACK makes the round trips longer than the queue does) and a window
of 1000000 bytes. Observation: level 2, at the first slow-start threshold, the largest window was at least
100000 bytes (about 96 segments, more than 34 + 30).

%# parameter: TcpVegas.gamma
%# class: other
%# value: 30
%# key: *.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.gamma
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpVegasGammaOther")
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host1.tcp").signal("cwnd")
                                        .captureMax("cwndMax", "value")
                                        .within(3.0)))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("ssthresh")
                  .filterValueAtMost(1e8)
                  .first()
                  .assertModule("host1.tcp.conn-*", "{cwndMax} >= 100000")
                  .describe("the slow-start threshold at the end of slow start")
                  .within(2.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpVegasGammaOther compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.gamma = 30    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "TcpVegas"
network = inet.protocoltest.TapRouterNetwork
*.linkDelay = 5ms
*.bottleneckDatarate = 10Mbps
*.bottleneckDelay = 10ms
*.host2.tcp.delayedAcksEnabled = false
*.host2.tcp.advertisedWindow = 1000000
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 10000000B
sim-time-limit = 3.5s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpVegasGammaOther: PASS
